+# ADHOC.canon-r11-orion-reader-trail (MDPF_CANON CN-r-3 / E4 follow-up; dell1 CTO ruling 4F7E, msg 6965): S3 SERVER
+# ACCESS LOGGING to name the reader of the opal-data-assets/orion/ burst (REST.GET.OBJECT lines carry the requester,
+# source IP and user agent). One-time named measurement, NOT a standing monitor. TIME-BOXED: REMOVE this resource
+# within 72 hours of the apply, or as soon as the reader is named. The target bucket's policy admits this one source
+# through the opsec root (s3_access_logs.tf), and loses that line when this resource is removed.
+resource "aws_s3_bucket_logging" "monolith_orion_reader" {
+  bucket        = aws_s3_bucket.monolith.id
+  target_bucket = "opal-data-security-access-logs"
+  target_prefix = "opal-data-assets/"
+}
